---
code: dorc-sh-script-unreadable
when-fires: dorc-sh could not read the script it was handed. cli/bin/dorc-sh.rs. {path} and PASSTHROUGH {detail}.
why: dorc-sh is the shebang runner, so an unreadable script is the whole invocation failing before any strip or exec - reported as itself rather than as a shell error.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- dorc-sh-script-unreadable && mise run loom:promote -- dorc-sh-script-unreadable`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all dorc-sh-script-unreadable` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=webhost.sh
error[dorc-sh-script-unreadable]: sm cannot read webhost.sh: No such file or
directory (os error 2)
